# Listening to rewilding at The Deerstone

This small, **synthetic** field study is set at The Deerstone in County Wicklow, where MIRA held its inaugural gathering. It is designed to demonstrate a complete discourse graph in one readable document; the observations below are illustrative, not measurements made at the property.

The example asks whether areas under rewilded planting host more bird activity at dawn than nearby managed areas. Its question, protocol, claim, evidence, and request are authored as Stencila ResearchObjects and exported as a MIRA graph.

:::{question} Does rewilded planting support a richer dawn chorus?
:id: dawn-question
:label: Question 1
:addressed-by: #dawn-claim

Is bird acoustic activity greater around rewilded planting than around nearby managed grassland during the dawn chorus?

:::

:::{protocol} A paired dawn acoustic survey
:id: dawn-protocol
:label: Protocol 1

Place identical acoustic recorders at **four fixed locations**: two beside rewilded planting and two beside managed grassland. Record the same ten-minute window around local sunrise on two rain-free mornings.

Keep gain, orientation, and classifier settings fixed. For each recording, count candidate bird taxa and discrete call events; retain the audio so detections can be checked manually.

:::

:::{claim} Rewilded locations have greater dawn bird activity
:id: dawn-claim
:label: Claim 1
:supported-by: #acoustic-evidence
:opposed-by: #weather-evidence

In this illustrative pilot, locations beside rewilded planting show **more call events** and more candidate bird taxa than the managed locations.

:::

:::{evidence} Acoustic detections favour rewilded locations
:id: acoustic-evidence
:label: Evidence 1
:is-grounded-in: https://example.org/studies/deerstone-dawn-pilot

Across the four illustrative recordings in each habitat, the rewilded locations have a higher mean call-event count and more candidate taxa.

```csv
habitat,recordings,mean_call_events,candidate_taxa
rewilded,4,31,9
managed,4,18,6
```

:::

:::{evidence} The pilot is too short to separate habitat from conditions
:id: weather-evidence
:label: Evidence 2
:is-grounded-in: https://example.org/studies/deerstone-dawn-pilot

Only two mornings were sampled. Differences in wind, recorder placement, and automated classification could explain some or all of the apparent habitat effect, so the result should be treated as _provisional_.

:::

:::{request} Repeat the survey through the breeding season
:id: seasonal-request
:label: Request 1
:request-target: #dawn-claim
:request-for: https://example.org/studies/deerstone-seasonal-replication

Repeat the paired survey monthly from March to June, balance recorder positions between habitats, record local weather, and manually validate a stratified sample of detections.

:::
